1
00:00:00,913 --> 00:00:07,120
hFull

2
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:29,697
I'm so proud to be here.

3
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:31,540
Yeah, that's what I'm doing.

4
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:35,220
I'm so proud to be here.

5
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:39,157
I'm so proud

6
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:44,840
to be here.

7
00:00:51,140 --> 00:00:53,000
I'll take a break.

8
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:33,637
The only way we could stop Ken
was to defeat our friend Agumon.

9
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:37,737
We found the Digi-Egg of Friendship, but
Flymon found us and captured Patamon.

10
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:38,937
We all chased after him,

11
00:01:39,020 --> 00:01:42,477
but it led us right into MetalGreymon
with Ken riding the controls.

12
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:44,477
Koromon arrived and freed Patamon,

13
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:47,157
but no one could remove the
Dark Spiral from MetalGreymon.

14
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:50,417
Davis was still having a problem
fighting his Digimon friend,

15
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:52,197
but we convinced him that
sometimes friends have

16
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:54,357
to make sacrifices for
the sake of friendship.

17
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:56,757
Just then, the Digi-Egg
friendship activated,

18
00:01:56,840 --> 00:01:59,337
and Paildramon destroyed the
dark spirals on MetalGreymon

19
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:02,126
and allowed him to
digivolve back into Agumon.

20
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:31,180
Uh, nice serve, Gwen.

21
00:02:31,420 --> 00:02:32,717
I'm feeling a little dizzy.

22
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:34,212
I'd better take a break.

23
00:02:34,340 --> 00:02:35,170
Whatever.

24
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:37,541
Actually, why don't you two play?

25
00:02:40,740 --> 00:02:41,570
Huh?

26
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:46,155
Uh, nice serve, Gwen.

27
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:51,372
Beumon's in trouble, but how
will I get to the Digi-World?

28
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:55,190
Sora!

29
00:02:58,620 --> 00:03:00,267
I've got to tell the others.

30
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:07,100
That cabinet rinse makes
my ears look too stiff.

31
00:03:09,480 --> 00:03:11,000
So, ready to go?

32
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:13,188
Rome wasn't built in a day.

33
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:14,537
Looking beautiful takes time.

34
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:15,450
So beautiful.

35
00:03:15,540 --> 00:03:16,657
Can you help me wash the dishes?

36
00:03:16,740 --> 00:03:17,570
Tides up.

37
00:03:18,880 --> 00:03:20,645
Why are your ears standing up?

38
00:03:20,760 --> 00:03:21,697
It's a new look.

39
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:23,517
It's quite deraging, Kathmandu.

40
00:03:23,600 --> 00:03:26,012
You know, most cats like mice, not moose.

41
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:35,920
Ah, my stomach is full.

42
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:38,652
You shouldn't eat so much in the morning.

43
00:03:38,780 --> 00:03:40,520
You ate twice as much as me.

44
00:03:40,720 --> 00:03:43,779
If you keep it up, you'll
digivolve into heavy mine.

45
00:03:44,820 --> 00:03:45,650
Huh?

46
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:47,920
Biyomon. Hmm?

47
00:03:48,940 --> 00:03:51,640
An emergency call from Biyomon? What's up?

48
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:56,380
It's Biyomon.

49
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:57,638
She needs our help.

50
00:03:58,040 --> 00:04:00,099
That's nothing to shake a stick at.

51
00:04:07,260 --> 00:04:11,142
Note to self, think a better way
to sneak Upamon out of apartment.

52
00:04:15,820 --> 00:04:18,020
Hey, be more careful next time.

53
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:19,657
Cody, what have you been eating lately?

54
00:04:19,740 --> 00:04:21,197
You must have gained 20 pounds.

55
00:04:21,280 --> 00:04:22,110
It's Upamon.

56
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:24,840
You ate Upamon? Forget it.

57
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,706
Sora sent an email saying
Beamon's in trouble.

58
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:29,434
Your tummy's growling.

59
00:04:34,080 --> 00:04:37,037
The only way not to look
suspicious is to sneak quietly.

60
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:37,950
Right.

61
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,200
It's about time.

62
00:04:43,300 --> 00:04:44,130
Where's TK and Kari?

63
00:04:44,213 --> 00:04:46,062
It wasn't my turn to watch them.

64
00:04:47,100 --> 00:04:48,480
No TK or Kari?

65
00:04:48,660 --> 00:04:51,954
Even if they were out of town,
at least they'd email us.

66
00:04:52,220 --> 00:04:54,338
Mmm, that milkshake was really good.

67
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:57,618
But seeing you drink through
a straw was even better.

68
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:02,005
Now we can take some pictures.

69
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:03,150
No, wait.

70
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:05,360
The fish market's calling my name.

71
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:06,960
All right.

72
00:05:17,260 --> 00:05:19,460
Hmm, maybe their batteries are dead.

73
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:21,977
Maybe TK decided to wash in the bathtub.

74
00:05:22,060 --> 00:05:23,120
We can't wait.

75
00:05:23,340 --> 00:05:24,420
Biyomon needs us.

76
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:26,497
We'll just have to go without them.

77
00:05:26,580 --> 00:05:27,410
Right.

78
00:05:27,493 --> 00:05:29,837
Let's see exactly where Biomon's
distress signal came from.

79
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:31,800
There it is. Got it.

80
00:05:33,660 --> 00:05:36,437
Well, now that we know where we need
to get, let's get to getting to it.

81
00:05:36,520 --> 00:05:37,350
Got it?

82
00:05:37,433 --> 00:05:38,263
Right.

83
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:41,316
All right, everyone.

84
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:42,620
Digiport open!

85
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:57,560
Oh, Bulb, I sense this
place is a cultural desert.

86
00:05:57,780 --> 00:05:58,956
Did you say dessert?

87
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:02,560
This sandblasting sure makes
my shell look real shiny.

88
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:12,800
Wow, check it out!

89
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:15,577
Looks like the Old West.

90
00:06:15,660 --> 00:06:17,737
Where's that spire we saw on the monitor?

91
00:06:17,820 --> 00:06:19,996
I don't see a control spire anywhere.

92
00:06:20,420 --> 00:06:21,832
What are we waiting for?

93
00:06:22,460 --> 00:06:26,917
Fear not, Yoli, for I will guard you from
whatever danger may be thrust upon us.

94
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:30,397
Instead of guarding my life,
try finding us some cold water.

95
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:31,310
Huh?

96
00:06:31,780 --> 00:06:32,697
Where's Biomar?

97
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:34,437
She can't have gone far, Davis.

98
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:35,755
She's here somewhere.

99
00:06:36,740 --> 00:06:38,297
Where's that music coming from?

100
00:06:38,380 --> 00:06:39,737
It's coming from over there.

101
00:06:39,820 --> 00:06:41,879
That's when there's a Gila monster.

102
00:06:43,180 --> 00:06:44,337
How do you like that?

103
00:06:44,420 --> 00:06:45,717
It's just a player piano.

104
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:47,797
I'm starting to think
that there's nobody here.

105
00:06:47,880 --> 00:06:48,760
I don't know.

106
00:06:49,140 --> 00:06:49,997
You're at the right place.

107
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:51,517
You're set just where you are.

108
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:55,247
You're sure to be happy here,
so says the mon behind the star.

109
00:06:56,400 --> 00:06:57,230
Howdy.

110
00:06:57,313 --> 00:07:00,512
Welcome, Digi-Pilgrims, to the
safest town west of Cirrus.

111
00:07:00,620 --> 00:07:02,000
They call me Starmon.

112
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:05,757
Starmon is a law and order
Digimon who keeps the peace.

113
00:07:05,840 --> 00:07:06,917
But if you break the law,

114
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:10,477
his powerful meteor shower will
rain down swift justice upon you.

115
00:07:10,560 --> 00:07:15,501
Now belly up to the bar so I can welcome
all of you with a cold mug of welcome milk.

116
00:07:15,740 --> 00:07:16,570
Huh?

117
00:07:16,653 --> 00:07:18,097
Didn't spill a drop, did I?

118
00:07:18,180 --> 00:07:20,597
This is just my way of being
neighborly to strangers.

119
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:21,739
So, here's to you.

120
00:07:21,960 --> 00:07:23,489
Just what is welcome milk?

121
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:26,920
It's 100 % homogenized
moo juice, little missy.

122
00:07:27,820 --> 00:07:28,650
Welcome.

123
00:07:33,660 --> 00:07:35,937
Now that you mention
it, I'm kind of thirsty.

124
00:07:36,020 --> 00:07:39,017
My mouth feels like a clothes
dryer full of cotton balls.

125
00:07:39,100 --> 00:07:40,982
My tongue is a dusty tank tread.

126
00:07:41,340 --> 00:07:42,220
Thank you.

127
00:07:45,440 --> 00:07:47,205
Tourists, you gotta love them.

128
00:07:47,760 --> 00:07:48,590
Huh?

129
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:50,440
Uh, Mr. Starmon,

130
00:07:50,700 --> 00:07:52,737
have you by any chance
seen a cute little pink

131
00:07:52,820 --> 00:07:55,526
bird-looking Digimon
named Biyomon around here?

132
00:07:55,980 --> 00:07:57,880
Hmm, did you say Biyomon?

133
00:07:58,200 --> 00:07:59,729
That kind of rings a bell.

134
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:04,268
Yep, yep, I got a feeling I've
heard that description before.

135
00:08:07,940 --> 00:08:08,770
Beumon wanted?

136
00:08:08,980 --> 00:08:09,921
What did she do?

137
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:14,864
Well, that Digi-Desperado is on
the run from the Digimon Emperor.

138
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:18,257
He's got a reward out for her,
but they haven't caught her yet.

139
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:20,737
Well, she's hopefully
somewhere safe by now,

140
00:08:20,820 --> 00:08:23,197
but I'll still feel a lot
better when we find her.

141
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:24,110
Mr.

142
00:08:24,193 --> 00:08:25,217
Starmon, sir, maybe you could help.

143
00:08:25,300 --> 00:08:27,437
We heard she was last seen near here.

144
00:08:27,520 --> 00:08:29,897
You couldn't be more
right about that, ma 'am.

145
00:08:29,980 --> 00:08:31,917
And if Beumon were in
trouble, you'd help her.

146
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:36,353
Being a Leomon, I know you'd protect
her from that digital emperor, right?

147
00:08:37,420 --> 00:08:39,949
Ma 'am, there's something
I gotta tell you.

148
00:08:40,480 --> 00:08:41,310
Huh?

149
00:08:41,393 --> 00:08:42,351
He's wearing a dark ring!

150
00:08:42,960 --> 00:08:43,790
Well,

151
00:08:43,873 --> 00:08:46,577
I knew that behind that kin
star was just a gutless,

152
00:08:46,660 --> 00:08:49,537
low-life lackey of the emperor
with jelly for a spine.

153
00:08:49,620 --> 00:08:52,317
You could have told us, and what
do we say about name-calling?

154
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:54,477
Looks like the jury's
still out on Starmon.

155
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:56,197
Think he's a bad apple or a good one?

156
00:08:56,280 --> 00:08:57,417
People are like milk.

157
00:08:57,500 --> 00:08:58,330
They can turn bad.

158
00:08:58,413 --> 00:08:59,260
You're right.

159
00:08:59,520 --> 00:09:02,477
You might think I'm lower than
a snake's belly for saying this,

160
00:09:02,560 --> 00:09:05,384
but I do work for the
Emperor, and I got orders.

161
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:08,420
Hunt them down and
punish the Digidestined.

162
00:09:09,460 --> 00:09:11,977
What's that Earth Reject doing
now, pulling wings off butterflies?

163
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:15,060
You can bet he's experimenting
with something evil.

164
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:17,120
It's almost finished.

165
00:09:20,620 --> 00:09:21,580
Earth Reject.

166
00:09:21,740 --> 00:09:26,152
I'll have to use that at the next
company picnic and team-building seminar.

167
00:09:26,700 --> 00:09:27,900
Don't that beat all.

168
00:09:28,060 --> 00:09:29,060
Trying to escape.

169
00:09:30,460 --> 00:09:32,960
No use trying to hot tail it out of here.

170
00:09:33,220 --> 00:09:34,749
Time for a weather report.

171
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:36,320
Meteor shower!

172
00:09:41,940 --> 00:09:44,800
I learned heavy showers,
but that was too much.

173
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:47,120
Now you'll enjoy your stay.

174
00:09:49,340 --> 00:09:50,340
Here's the rules.

175
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:51,677
No cookies in your cell.

176
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:52,877
No loud music after eight.

177
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:55,317
and no shucking oysters
during months without an R.

178
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:56,230
Enjoy!

179
00:09:56,540 --> 00:09:57,900
No way!

180
00:09:59,740 --> 00:10:00,620
Zahra!

181
00:10:01,900 --> 00:10:02,730
Huh?

182
00:10:02,920 --> 00:10:03,880
What was that?

183
00:10:04,780 --> 00:10:05,660
Zahra!

184
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:07,720
Beumon!

185
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:29,200
I tried to get away, but I
just didn't have the strength.

186
00:10:29,640 --> 00:10:31,060
Shh, don't talk.

187
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:32,280
What happened?

188
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:37,480
You just said don't talk, didn't you?

189
00:10:37,780 --> 00:10:39,940
I wish you would make up your mind.

190
00:10:40,980 --> 00:10:42,880
Kay, you can talk a little.

191
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:46,000
When I first came here to this town,

192
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:49,671
I had no idea that it was under
the control of the Emperor.

193
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:54,580
I had been shot down by his
flying dragons and needed food.

194
00:10:54,900 --> 00:10:57,135
I was tired, hungry, and very thirsty.

195
00:10:57,400 --> 00:10:58,560
Welcome, stranger.

196
00:10:59,100 --> 00:10:59,930
Huh?

197
00:11:00,013 --> 00:11:01,660
Your throat must be parched.

198
00:11:01,860 --> 00:11:03,684
How about a cold drink of milk?

199
00:11:03,920 --> 00:11:04,877
Well, how nice.

200
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:06,377
You're right, I am thirsty.

201
00:11:06,460 --> 00:11:08,284
Thank you for your hospitality.

202
00:11:10,360 --> 00:11:11,400
Meteor shower!

203
00:11:20,900 --> 00:11:22,665
I'm glad you can stay a while.

204
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:29,000
V, headbutt!

205
00:11:29,840 --> 00:11:32,960
I guess I used too much V
and not enough headbutt.

206
00:11:33,700 --> 00:11:34,641
Nice try, buddy.

207
00:11:35,140 --> 00:11:37,677
That wall's as hard as his
head and just as thick.

208
00:11:37,760 --> 00:11:38,640
You said it.

209
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:41,777
But it should be easy for you
to drill through that wall.

210
00:11:41,860 --> 00:11:43,154
Digivolve into Digmon.

211
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:45,720
I'm too weak to do it. I forgot.

212
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:46,880
We haven't eaten.

213
00:11:47,220 --> 00:11:49,279
I could do something if I had food.

214
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:53,277
Boy, Yoli, I sure wish we had
some snacks from your store.

215
00:11:53,360 --> 00:11:54,190
I'll call my dad.

216
00:11:54,273 --> 00:11:55,103
He delivers.

217
00:11:55,186 --> 00:11:57,960
But, Yoli, we're in prison
in the digital world.

218
00:11:58,120 --> 00:11:58,950
You're right.

219
00:11:59,033 --> 00:12:01,177
If it's more than five miles,
there's a delivery charge.

220
00:12:01,260 --> 00:12:02,820
Huh? What, Biyomon?

221
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:04,800
It sounds like a horse.

222
00:12:12,300 --> 00:12:13,860
He needs some new shoes.

223
00:12:15,260 --> 00:12:16,540
I said, whoa!

224
00:12:17,180 --> 00:12:20,240
Never fear, the protector
of justice is here.

225
00:12:20,560 --> 00:12:23,760
Holy guacamole, just who
in tarnation are you?

226
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:27,100
Howdy, folks.

227
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:32,017
Deputy Mon is a barrel-chested
Digimon that shoots from the lip,

228
00:12:32,100 --> 00:12:34,335
but usually he's helpful and harmless.

229
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:42,257
From the look on your faces, I feel
like I squashed your favorite hat.

230
00:12:42,340 --> 00:12:45,657
We got put in this jail for doing
nothing by your partner, Star Mon.

231
00:12:45,740 --> 00:12:46,975
Where's your justice?

232
00:12:47,180 --> 00:12:49,497
Yeah, that's all that's in here, just us.

233
00:12:49,580 --> 00:12:50,410
So let's see it.

234
00:12:50,493 --> 00:12:51,557
Where's your dark ring, deputy?

235
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:54,228
Well, see for yourself,
I ain't got no ring.

236
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:56,640
Nobody controls me, not even myself.

237
00:12:57,200 --> 00:12:58,435
There's no dark ring.

238
00:12:58,580 --> 00:13:00,260
Right toe, you varmints.

239
00:13:01,460 --> 00:13:06,620
We're sorry to be so suspicious of you,
deputy mon, but put yourself in our boots.

240
00:13:06,820 --> 00:13:08,820
There, you see any rings now?

241
00:13:11,340 --> 00:13:12,840
Got carried away.

242
00:13:13,280 --> 00:13:14,357
We didn't see a thing.

243
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:18,317
Uh, Deputy Mon, are you here to
keep us in jail or to set us free?

244
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:19,740
No need to fret, lady.

245
00:13:19,900 --> 00:13:21,076
Soon you'll be free.

246
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:22,190
Yay!

247
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:26,180
Of course, I'm only
freeing the girls. Huh?

248
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:30,460
I need card players, but not boys,
because they cheat. Say what?

249
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:32,957
Did I mention I don't
even cheat at solitaire?

250
00:13:33,040 --> 00:13:34,857
Strictly womenfolk, and that's final.

251
00:13:34,940 --> 00:13:37,317
Didn't you ever hear of women,
children, and Digimon first?

252
00:13:37,400 --> 00:13:38,697
Couldn't you find it in
your heart to make an

253
00:13:38,780 --> 00:13:41,677
exception and let us all
go just for the fun of it?

254
00:13:41,760 --> 00:13:43,740
Come on, ladies only. Scoot.

255
00:13:46,760 --> 00:13:48,960
What is this, the petrified desert?

256
00:13:49,140 --> 00:13:50,220
I said, Scoop!

257
00:13:50,680 --> 00:13:52,500
But we're not, boys! Move!

258
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:54,840
Giddy up, cellophane!

259
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:04,260
Well, it's lunchtime.

260
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:07,620
